{"parentUuid":"a1b2c3d4-0007-4a35-9d77-69bb271400b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo conventions worth remembering: first, run every command through uv run so the lockfile stays authoritative, plain python will drift the environment. Second, the integration suite needs the local docker compose stack, start it with docker compose up -d postgres redis before running pytest tests/integration. Third, never edit the generated client under src/gen, regenerate it from the OpenAPI spec with make client instead. Fourth, commit messages follow the conventional commits style and every commit must include the regression test that pinpoints the bug it fixes. Fifth, the benchmarks gate merges, if the perf suite regresses more than three percent the pipeline blocks the pull request until an owner signs off on the numbers. Sixth, keep the changelog entry in the same pull request as the user visible change."},"sessionId":"f617f58f-40f9-4a35-9d77-69bb271400b2","type":"user","uuid":"a1b2c3d4-0008-4a35-9d77-69bb271400b2","timestamp":"2026-09-01T19:43:00.000Z","cwd":"/Users/rom.iluz/Dev/example","gitBranch":"main","userType":"external","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","promptId":"p_0002"}
